WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.604 --> 00:00:13.115
A linear stage delivers what it receives multiplied by a gain: its transfer curve is a straight line. Hard clipping flattens everything past the limit.

2
00:00:13.499 --> 00:00:20.951
Soft saturation bends the transfer curve gradually, like a tube or tape: it rounds the peaks instead of cutting them.

3
00:00:21.646 --> 00:00:31.000
Clipping a sine symmetrically adds odd harmonics: the third, the fifth, the seventh. The wave looks more and more like a square.

4
00:00:36.054 --> 00:00:45.664
Total harmonic distortion compares the energy of the harmonics with that of the fundamental. A pure sine has zero percent; a square, 48 percent.
